WEBVTT

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:04.610
You should be fine now.

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:06.760
It's all thanks to you, Doctor.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:15.150
Now if Miss Illy will allow us to examine 
her, we'll be able to return to Lindworm.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:15.740
Yes.

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.360
But she's rejecting an examination.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.370
I wonder if I did something wrong.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.690
Doctor.

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:25.170
I actually wanted to discuss 
that matter with you.

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:32.660
She's requesting to see Miss Tisalia 
in exchange for the examination?

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.460
Do you two know each other?

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:36.880
We do not.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.920
I haven't the slightest idea 
as to why Illy requested this.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.280
That's where Illy is, right?

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.320
Illy, I'm coming in.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:02.960
So you came?

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:14.180
<b>Monster Girl Doctor</b>

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:37.010
Case 6        The Harpy Who Couldn't Fly

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:38.350
It's been a while. Do you remember me?

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:40.310
I'm the doctor who examined you back—

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:41.230
I remember you.

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:43.350
Have you been doing okay?

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:45.970
I heard you've been losing 
feathers and can no longer fly.

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:47.830
Do I look okay to you?

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:51.340
My apologies. That may have 
been a dumb question.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:54.720
Is that Tisalia?

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:57.530
It is. You wanted to talk to her?

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:58.960
Yeah.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.510
Do you mind if I examine you first?

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:04.220
May I see your wings?

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:09.490
<i>Compared to other harpies, 
the colors aren't as vibrant,</i>

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:12.210
<i>but they're pretty big for her body.</i>

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:14.330
<i>She's probably a great flyer.</i>

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:18.910
No problems. I'm going to 
touch a bit further in.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:23.200
Did that hurt?

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.280
It's nothing I can't handle.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:27.620
May I pull on your feathers a bit?

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.310
Do whatever you want.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:35.360
May I touch your head, too?

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:41.730
That tickles!

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:43.570
Bear with it for just a bit.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:49.880
And now, finally...

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:56.950
I-I was just trying to 
take your temperature...

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:58.700
W-Warn me first!

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.480
Doctor...

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:02.800
M-May I try one more time?

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:07.530
Why don't you use a mercury thermometer?

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:10.310
They break easily, and 
they're not very accurate.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:12.960
I've found this to be the most reliable method.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:18.040
Sorry, please don't move. I won't 
be able to get a proper reading.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.570
Your hands are cold!

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:24.810
I'm not surprised my hands feel cold to you. 
Harpies have a higher body temperature.

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:32.320
37.8 degrees Celsius. 
Your temperature is fine.

00:04:33.270 --> 00:04:34.700
Doctor.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:39.210
How many times must I tell you 
to be gentler with young girls?

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:42.310
Doctor! Are you all right?!

00:04:42.310 --> 00:04:45.100
You're always so violent, snake woman.

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.590
You're the last one I want to 
hear that from, horse woman.

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:51.010
Not in front of the patient, you two...

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:55.010
Doctor, what kind of sickness do I have?

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:57.690
Illy, you're...

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:01.710
actually not sick at all.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:03.150
You're just molting.

00:05:04.450 --> 00:05:05.570
Huh?

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:10.070
You always grow new feathers 
when the seasons change, right?

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:11.570
This is the same thing.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:14.400
There's no sign that the 
feather loss is due to stress,

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:17.320
and you don't have a skin disease 
or any external injuries.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:19.910
As long as you eat well and get enough rest, you'll be able to fly in no—

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:21.080
You're lying!

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:24.700
I'm not lying, though. You're not sick...

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:29.430
That can't be true! Even when 
I molted before, I could still fly!

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:33.180
You just happened to lose more 
feathers than usual this time.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:36.260
It's pretty common for harpies 
to be unable to fly when molti—

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:40.290
You're wrong! There has to be 
a bigger reason why I can't fly!

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:41.100
But...

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:42.860
Forget it!

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.640
Never mind, you quack!

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:49.510
I wish I'd never met you! Get out!

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:50.740
All of you get out!

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:53.410
Illy, please calm down and listen to me.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:05.630
This little bird needs to 
watch where her feet go.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:09.950
Don't you have something to say to him?

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:15.990
Illy, wait!

00:06:16.530 --> 00:06:18.270
Well, that's not good.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:22.220
It's not unusual for you to 
lack delicacy, but still...

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:23.980
I never imagined she'd be that angry.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:28.270
Harpies tend to get overzealous when 
they're preoccupied with one specific thing.

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:31.700
The way she was acting, 
there's no telling where she might go.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.240
Yeah, let's follow her.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:36.870
Doctor, please allow me to handle this.

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:50.820
There you are.

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:56.860
What, you came alone?

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:58.960
You wanted a word with me, did you not?

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:02.620
Then just come out and say so 
rather than playing these little games.

00:07:02.620 --> 00:07:06.250
Well, the elder said I couldn't 
see you unless I got examined.

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:08.850
I see. So what did you want?

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:12.100
You're a gladiator at the arena, right?

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.230
Indeed, I am.

00:07:14.230 --> 00:07:17.850
I used to go watch matches 
at the arena all the time.

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:21.600
Did you know you can watch 
matches for free from the roof?

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:25.790
I'm perfectly fine if you don't pay, so long 
as you don't take up a seat in the audience.

00:07:25.790 --> 00:07:29.200
I wanna become a gladiator like you!

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:32.300
You always shone so brightly 
when you were competing!

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:34.730
I never knew your name, though.

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:38.890
I'd thank you if you were a fan, 
but I somehow doubt that is the case.

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:42.670
I'm not your fan, but I wanna 
be able to battle like you.

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:46.290
The arena welcomes everyone.

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:49.810
But mere idolization will 
not be enough to get you—

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:50.900
I'll do it, though!

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:54.330
I grew up in the slums.

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:56.250
I'm awesome at fighting!

00:07:57.330 --> 00:07:58.980
Fighting, you say?

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:00.370
Huh?

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:06.970
We are not merely fighting at the arena.

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:09.580
It is a contest of dexterity 
and elegance of technique.

00:08:10.700 --> 00:08:14.010
Still, whoever clobbers their 
opponent in the end wins, right?

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:18.130
Incorrect! I'm telling you that 
it's a matter of character!

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.580
Character?

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:24.210
Very well.

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:36.500
I shall see if your "fighting" is good enough.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:40.330
Ooh, are we fighting? 
Hell yeah! Let's do this!

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:42.340
Don't come crying to me if you get hurt.

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:52.510
The first thing gladiators need is etiquette.

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:57.670
A little girl like you, who called the 
doctor who saved you from slavers a quack,

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:00.590
shall be raked across the coals.

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:04.430
You went a bit overboard, didn't you?

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:08.010
Ouch! That stings...

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:09.560
Just bear with me a bit.

00:09:10.030 --> 00:09:12.330
Does Illy know anything about combat?

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:15.540
No, she just used underhanded tricks.

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:18.460
And yet she managed to 
strike you in the face.

00:09:18.840 --> 00:09:21.110
Her talon only scratched my face.

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:25.260
Though I made sure to give her quite 
the drubbing with that wooden pole.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:31.320
I'm hoping I don't have to worry about this, 
but you did go easy on her, right?

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:34.520
But of course! I was just 
putting her in her place.

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:36.900
Though I may have let my pride overcome me.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:38.950
Why bother getting into a rivalry with her?

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:44.050
Well, it just infuriated me when 
she spoke badly of the doctor.

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:46.640
I do share your opinion on that.

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:51.240
I've been pondering how I can get that 
harpy girl to take some anesthetic.

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:53.110
Th-That's going too far!

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:55.110
I jest.

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:58.240
Anyway, we can't just leave Illy alone.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:09:59.600
We have to do something.

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:02.360
Yes, well...

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:12.460
Do you now understand that your 
"fighting" is not good enough?

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:16.340
Forget becoming a gladiator. 
Just live peacefully in this village.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:18.600
I can't stay here forever!

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:22.080
But why not? Everyone here is so kind.

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:27.570
They're all nice people... 
but something feels wrong here.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:29.530
Then where would you prefer to be?

00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:30.890
Ugh, I don't know!

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:35.770
But I'm sure if I got somewhere else, I'd...

00:10:36.830 --> 00:10:41.850
Whatever is plaguing her is something 
she will have to resolve on her own.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:45.330
Illy never made an effort to fit in.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:48.860
Whenever she didn't like something, 
she would just run away.

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:51.770
Then when she said she wanted
to become a gladiator...

00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:54.750
It was just an excuse to leave this village.

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:58.120
Even if she did become a gladiator, 
I'm sure she'd just run away again.

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:00.250
She'd just fly off into the 
sky and never look back.

00:11:00.770 --> 00:11:07.210
I guess once Illy is done molting and able to 
fly again, she may actually leave this village.

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:12.980
But if that happens, who knows when she'll 
be kidnapped by monster slavers again?

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:16.950
By the way, Doctor...

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:21.370
Here's a feather that she lost during our bout.

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:24.890
I picked it up because it was rather large.

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:28.360
This is a flight feather.

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:33.290
I hope this will aid you 
with her examination.

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:36.500
Could you two help me 
with something tomorrow?

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:37.440
Huh?

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:38.760
But of course.

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:42.330
O-Of course I will!

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:43.880
Thank you both.

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:49.730
I'd like to conduct a little treasure hunt.

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:54.000
<b>Monster Girl Doctor</b>

00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:03.270
Here's one.

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:11.250
I ran around the village and gathered 
feathers that matched Illy's.

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:15.990
Thank you for your help. 
If this means what I think it means...

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:17.800
Is she ill, then?

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:21.360
No. She's molting.

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:23.170
I'm sure of that.

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:26.530
Not even a hint of doubt 
in your face, Doctor.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:33.690
Illy mentioned that there must
be somewhere she belongs.

00:12:34.130 --> 00:12:35.740
Where might that be?

00:12:35.740 --> 00:12:38.940
I'm not certain. I assume it's somewhere...

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:42.680
Somewhere she can find something 
she couldn't find here.

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:44.450
I'm sure that's what she believes.

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:47.950
Though in the end, 
she's just fleeing from reality.

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:53.410
Still, only she can understand the 
anguish caused by her inability to fly.

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:58.530
I only know how to clobber bad 
little girls into submission.

00:12:58.530 --> 00:13:03.760
But with your knowledge and talent, 
you can save her, Doctor.

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:05.040
I'm sure of it.

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:11.050
Here you are, Good Doctor. 
I've brought what you asked for.

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:13.490
That's way too many, Sapphee.

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:16.400
All of these can't possibly belong to Illy.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:21.580
Oh, I didn't notice. I was so distracted by 
the sound of you chatting the day away.

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:25.260
Miss Tisalia was just giving 
me a little confidence.

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:25.940
Heavens!

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:29.200
I'm so honored to know I was 
useful to you, Doctor!

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:36.830
Congratulations, Miss Tisalia, though I'm 
useful to Dr. Glenn on a daily basis.

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:38.920
P-Please don't fight...

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:42.140
I'm going back to work.

00:13:42.140 --> 00:13:42.840
Sapphee...

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:45.690
I wonder if Miss Sapphee is tired.

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:48.050
This environment is rather unkind to lamias.

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:49.020
Huh?

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:51.710
It's very cold and windy in this village.

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:54.730
Make sure you give Miss Sapphee 
some attention, as well.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:56.280
Miss Tisalia...

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:02.600
I'll be more careful.

00:14:02.600 --> 00:14:03.450
Indeed.

00:14:04.640 --> 00:14:06.610
There you are, Dr. Glenn!

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:08.130
Is there a medical emergency?

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:09.490
Well, not exactly.

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:11.740
We can't find Illy anywhere.

00:14:12.570 --> 00:14:14.490
She must've ventured outside the village.

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:15.810
Honestly, that girl...

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:16.630
We'll search for her.

00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:17.860
Right away!

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:21.960
<i>I've always loved flying.</i>

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:44.730
<i>I could go anywhere I wanted 
as long as I could fly.</i>

00:14:50.230 --> 00:14:54.310
<i>I could go on living as long 
as I could fly through the sky.</i>

00:14:54.310 --> 00:14:55.250
<i>But now...</i>

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:19.780
I still can't fly.

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:23.810
I can't go anywhere if I can't fly...

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:28.570
I thought that if I could become 
a gladiator, maybe then...

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:30.720
But I didn't stand a chance against her.

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:35.360
If only I could fly to the moon...

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:40.530
Even if you have wings, 
you cannot fly forever.

00:15:40.900 --> 00:15:44.530
There will come a day when you must land.

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:46.840
I know that.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:49.980
But where...

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:53.340
Where am I supposed to go?

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:58.060
Illy! Come out at once!

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:00.060
Where could she have gone?

00:16:04.490 --> 00:16:06.080
Doctor, I found her.

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:07.400
She's over there.

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:09.020
Thank you!

00:16:09.020 --> 00:16:11.500
I'm surprised you could see 
her from so far away...

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:14.670
Oh, it must be your ability 
to sense body heat.

00:16:14.670 --> 00:16:15.610
Indeed.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:20.310
Now, let us go fetch that 
troublesome little child.

00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:24.580
Just leave me alone!

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:29.210
I'm never going to be able to 
fly again! Just leave me alone!

00:16:29.210 --> 00:16:31.480
That is not an option.

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:34.210
You must apologize for worrying everyone.

00:16:34.210 --> 00:16:35.970
That's not happening!

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:37.970
Stop being so difficult!

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:40.990
It appears that she requires 
quite a bit of attention.

00:16:42.090 --> 00:16:44.590
What? Now the quack's here, too?

00:16:44.590 --> 00:16:48.480
There you go again, being 
rude to the good doc—

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:53.240
Listen to me, Illy! My diagnosis 
wasn't entirely accurate!

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.500
If I'm sick, just tell me!

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:58.790
I can never go anywhere again...

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:00.740
I don't care what happens to me anymore!

00:17:01.030 --> 00:17:03.910
You aren't losing feathers 
because you're sick!

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:05.700
You are indeed molting!

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:08.370
Take a look at this!

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:11.200
It's one of the flight feathers you lost.

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:13.550
Can you tell that it's red at the base?

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:17.420
Yeah, so what?! My wings have always been red!

00:17:17.420 --> 00:17:22.300
No, this isn't the same red as your wings. And...

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:29.270
Your feathers that we gathered from the 
village had other colors mixed in, too.

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:32.690
Th-Those are my feathers! How dare 
you go collecting them like that?!

00:17:33.140 --> 00:17:35.470
I apologize for collecting 
them without your permission.

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:38.330
But now I know why you can't fly!

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:52.580
Illy is not sick.

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:58.320
Why didn't I tell Glenn that?

00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:00.590
Well, it wouldn't be any fun if I did.

00:18:03.510 --> 00:18:08.850
Just like at the academy, you never 
know when you'll have a pop quiz.

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:14.310
Well, Glenn? Were you able 
to find the right answer?

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:20.860
Th-The reason I can't fly?

00:18:20.860 --> 00:18:23.620
It's because the molt 
you're going through now...

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:30.070
is a very special type of molting 
where you get your adult feathers.

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:33.300
Adult... feathers?

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:38.300
Yes. Your wings should be a bit different 
from those of other harpies now.

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:41.310
Because you have phoenix blood in you.

00:18:41.820 --> 00:18:44.130
Ph-Phoenix blood?

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:47.450
The phoenix.

00:18:48.450 --> 00:18:52.020
A legendary monster that is also 
known as the immortal bird.

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:54.770
Illy has its blood in her veins.

00:18:54.770 --> 00:19:00.420
Though that doesn't make Illy 
a legendary creature herself.

00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:06.370
But she did, at least, inherit the 
beautiful wings admired by all.

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:09.680
How did I figure it out?

00:19:09.680 --> 00:19:12.540
You do know that I'm the 
director here, do you not?

00:19:14.690 --> 00:19:20.130
I'm growing my adult feathers... 
and I'm related to the legendary phoenix?

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:23.590
You'll be able to fly again. I'm sure of it.

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:27.010
You'll continue to be reborn with beautiful, 
fiery wings, again and again!

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:36.770
You mean... I'll be able to...

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:40.690
fly again?

00:19:44.940 --> 00:19:46.920
Doctor, lookie!

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:50.800
Do any of them look out 
of place? Do I look okay?

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:54.170
I think some may need to grow in more, 
but they'll all grow back soon.

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:54.970
Don't worry.

00:19:58.270 --> 00:20:00.830
There you are, all scantily clad again.

00:20:01.280 --> 00:20:04.250
A girl should always take 
care of her appearance.

00:20:05.080 --> 00:20:08.520
Oh, whatever! I'm gonna get 
everyone to look at them!

00:20:09.170 --> 00:20:15.030
Just for future reference, why were you 
so guarded when I went to examine you?

00:20:17.130 --> 00:20:21.520
Well, um... that's because... you ...aw me...

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:24.530
Out with it already!

00:20:25.670 --> 00:20:29.410
Because you saw me lay my egg!

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:33.700
I-I'm gonna go show everyone else my wings!

00:20:38.720 --> 00:20:41.790
She seems to be feeling better.

00:20:42.140 --> 00:20:44.340
The elder was pretty surprised, too,

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:47.880
by how drastically her wings changed
just because she entered adulthood.

00:20:48.200 --> 00:20:50.730
Considering she was an orphan,

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:55.140
I'm sure it was paramount to Illy that she 
found out a little about her ancestry.

00:20:55.140 --> 00:20:56.820
I'm sure it was.

00:20:56.820 --> 00:20:59.850
Maybe I didn't even need 
to do anything after all.

00:20:59.850 --> 00:21:02.050
That's not true.

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:08.740
To a teenage girl, being told that she's going 
to be an adult now means a great deal.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:13.380
There really wasn't a somewhere else.

00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:11.910
Lookie!

00:21:13.380 --> 00:21:16.870
As long as she's here, 
this is where she belongs.

00:21:17.190 --> 00:21:22.500
Just like the centaurs who abandoned 
the battlefield so they could start anew.

00:21:33.010 --> 00:21:34.530
Is something the matter?

00:21:34.650 --> 00:21:37.940
N-No, it's nothing.

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:40.540
<i>It felt hot for a moment.</i>

00:21:40.540 --> 00:21:42.040
<i>That shouldn't be, though.</i>

00:21:42.670 --> 00:21:48.860
<i>Perhaps the flames of the legendary 
phoenix still burn strong within Illy.</i>

00:23:25.430 --> 00:23:29.010
What's this? Still not here?

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:33.580
I don't know how much longer I can behave...

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.010
Case 7         The Hedonistic Arachne

00:23:35.770 --> 00:23:38.860
Case 7: "The Hedonistic Arachne."
